<div class="max-w-4xl">
    <h2 id="w-actions" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-6 scroll-mt-24">Actions</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8">Every button is a <code>box</code> with a <code>click</code> handler and a text child &mdash; there is no button primitive. The variants differ only in their style roles.</p>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">button(label, on_click)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">The primary action. <code>on_click</code> names a server event.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">button("Save", "save")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px system-ui;border:1px solid transparent;background:#6366f1;color:#fff">Save</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">secondary_button(label, on_click)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">A raised surface rather than the accent role.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">secondary_button("Cancel", "cancel")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px system-ui;border:1px solid transparent;background:#2a2933;color:#e5e7eb;border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)">Cancel</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">danger_button(label, on_click)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">The <code>danger</code> role, for destructive actions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">danger_button("Delete account", "destroy")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px system-ui;border:1px solid transparent;background:#dc2626;color:#fff">Delete account</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">ghost_button(label, on_click)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">Text only until hovered. For tertiary actions in dense toolbars.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">ghost_button("Dismiss", "dismiss")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px system-ui;border:1px solid transparent;background:transparent;color:#c7d2fe">Dismiss</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">button_variant(label, on_click, bg, fg)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">The builder the others call. Reach for it when you need a role pair the variants do not cover.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">button_variant("Publish", "publish", "success.base", "success.on")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px system-ui;border:1px solid transparent;background:#16a34a;color:#fff">Publish</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">icon_button(label, on_click, props)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">A square button holding a single glyph. <code>props</code> ride back on the event.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">icon_button("✕", "close", {"id": row["id"]})</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px system-ui;border:1px solid transparent;background:#2a2933;color:#e5e7eb;padding:7px 10px">✕</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">loading_button(label, on_click, key)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">Swaps to a spinner while the round trip is in flight, keyed so the diff replaces only the label.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">loading_button("Import", "import", "import-btn")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px system-ui;border:1px solid transparent;background:#6366f1;color:#fff;opacity:.8"><span style="display:inline-block;width:11px;height:11px;border:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.4);border-top-color:#fff;border-radius:50%"></span>Import</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">local_button(label, program, after)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">Runs a verified bytecode program on the client <em>before</em> the round trip, then sends <code>after</code>. This is what makes a counter feel instant.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">local_button("+", "state.count += 1", "increment")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px system-ui;border:1px solid transparent;background:#6366f1;color:#fff;padding:7px 16px">+</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <h2 id="w-input" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-6 scroll-mt-24">Input</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8">Editable fields are the <code>input</code> and <code>textarea</code> primitives; everything else is composed. A field reports its value through the event it names.</p>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">input(value, on_change)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">A single-line field. The event fires per keystroke with the value in <code>params</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">input(state["email"], "email_changed")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px;width:220px"><div style="background:#1f1e26;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);border-radius:7px;padding:8px 10px;color:#e5e7eb;font:13px system-ui">alice@example.com</div></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">sized_input(value, on_change, width)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">The same field at a fixed width, for inline and grid editing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">sized_input(cell, "cell_changed", 120)</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <span class="text-gray-600 text-xs italic">no visual &mdash; behaviour only</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">field(label, value, on_change)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">A labelled input &mdash; <code>labelled</code> plus <code>input</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">field("Email", state["email"], "email_changed")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px;width:220px"><div style="color:#9ca3af;font:12px system-ui;margin-bottom:5px">Email</div><div style="background:#1f1e26;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);border-radius:7px;padding:8px 10px;color:#e5e7eb;font:13px system-ui">alice@example.com</div></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">form(children, submit_label, on_submit)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">Fields plus a submit button. There is no browser form post &mdash; submit is an ordinary event.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">form([
  field("Name", s["name"], "name_changed"),
  field("Email", s["email"], "email_changed")
], "Create", "create")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px;width:220px"><div style="color:#9ca3af;font:12px system-ui;margin-bottom:4px">Name</div><div style="background:#1f1e26;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);border-radius:7px;padding:7px 10px;color:#e5e7eb;font:13px system-ui;margin-bottom:9px">Alice</div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px system-ui;border:1px solid transparent;background:#6366f1;color:#fff">Create</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">checkbox(label, checked, on_toggle, props)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">A box, a tick and a label. <code>props</code> is how a row says which row it is.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">checkbox(item["title"], item["done"], "toggle", {"id": item["id"]})</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px;width:200px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:4px;background:#6366f1;color:#fff;font:11px system-ui;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center">✓</span><span style="color:#e5e7eb;font:13px system-ui">Ship the release</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">switch(label, on, on_toggle, props)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">A checkbox that reads as a setting rather than a selection.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">switch("Email alerts", s["alerts"], "toggle_alerts", {})</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px;width:200px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px"><span style="width:32px;height:18px;border-radius:9px;background:#6366f1;position:relative;display:inline-block"><span style="position:absolute;right:2px;top:2px;width:14px;height:14px;border-radius:7px;background:#fff"></span></span><span style="color:#e5e7eb;font:13px system-ui">Email alerts</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">slider(value, min, max, on_set)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">A track, a filled portion and a thumb, driven by pointer events.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">slider(s["volume"], 0, 100, "set_volume")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:14px;width:200px"><div style="height:4px;border-radius:2px;background:#33323d;position:relative"><div style="width:62%;height:4px;border-radius:2px;background:#6366f1"></div><span style="position:absolute;left:calc(62% - 7px);top:-5px;width:14px;height:14px;border-radius:7px;background:#fff"></span></div></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">select(options, value, open, on_toggle, on_pick)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">A closed trigger plus, when <code>open</code>, an <code>overlay</code> of options. Open state lives in your state, not the client.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">select(["Draft", "Live"], s["status"], s["open"], "toggle", "pick")</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <div style="background:#17161c;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:10px;padding:12px;width:200px"><div style="background:#1f1e26;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);border-radius:7px;padding:7px 10px;color:#e5e7eb;font:13px system-ui;display:flex;justify-content:space-between">Live<span style="color:#9ca3af;font:12px system-ui">▾</span></div><div style="margin-top:4px;background:#1f1e26;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);border-radius:7px;overflow:hidden"><div style="color:#e5e7eb;font:13px system-ui;padding:6px 10px">Draft</div><div style="color:#e5e7eb;font:13px system-ui;padding:6px 10px;background:#6366f1;color:#fff">Live</div></div></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">select_sized(options, value, open, on_toggle, on_pick, min_width, grow)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">The same control with explicit width behaviour, for toolbars and grids.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">select_sized(cols, v, open, "t", "p", 140, false)</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <span class="text-gray-600 text-xs italic">no visual &mdash; behaviour only</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">dropdown(anchor, content, open)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">Any node as the trigger, any tree as the panel. <code>select</code> is one use of it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0">
            <div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">dropdown(icon_button("⋯", "toggle", {}), menu(items, "pick"), s["open"])</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 flex items-center justify-center border-t md:border-t-0 md:border-l border-white/5">
                <span class="text-gray-600 text-xs italic">no visual &mdash; behaviour only</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">textarea(value, on_change, o = {})</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">The multi-line field, and the only editable kind the client has besides `input`. The same node in every respect but that kind, and the kind is what makes the client wrap the text, put the caret on the line the pointer landed on, and keep `Enter` for a newline instead of a submit.  `o["rows"]` is a f</p>
        </div>
<div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">textarea(state["draft"].to_s, "draft", {</code></pre>
<p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-3">Real use &mdash; <code>app/controllers/chat_controller.sl:2702</code></p>
</div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">radio(label, selected, on_pick, props, o = {})</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">A radio is a checkbox that cannot be unticked and knows about its neighbours: choosing one is choosing away from the others. So the *group* owns the value — there is no `checked` argument that a caller could set on two of them at once — and each button carries only what it stands for, in `props`, wh</p>
        </div>
<div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">radio(opt, opt == value, on_pick, {"value": opt, "group": name}, {"size": size, "disabled": disabled})</code></pre>
<p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-3">Real use &mdash; <code>eui_builders.sl (inside `radio_group`):760</code></p>
</div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
